# TRELYAN — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and MUST NEVER be committed.
# Per the repo's security rules, operational credentials live in the environment or a
# KMS — never in source, never in a committed file, never in a log or error string.
#
# The protocol code itself reads only FALCON_DET1024_LIB. DEPLOYER_MNEMONIC is used
# solely by the TestNet deployment tooling, and in CI it comes from a repository
# secret, not from a file.

# ── Native Falcon signer (required for signing / the byte-identity KAT) ─────────
# Absolute path to the deterministic Falcon-1024 shared library, built from the
# PINNED source (see PINNED_BUILD.md — commit ce15e75b, FALCON_FPEMU=1).
#
# There is deliberately NO cwd-relative default: a dlopen path containing a slash
# resolves against the process working directory, so a "./libfalcondet1024.so"
# fallback would let anything writable in cwd supply the keygen/sign core (CWE-426).
# Unset ⇒ the loader fails closed. Always give an ABSOLUTE path.
#
#   cc -O3 -fPIC -DFALCON_UNALIGNED=0 -fno-strict-aliasing -shared \
#      -o libfalcondet1024.so codec.c common.c falcon.c fft.c fpr.c keygen.c \
#         rng.c shake.c sign.c vrfy.c deterministic.c
#
# Use a library built from the pinned tree: a divergent build breaks signature
# byte-identity, which for a DETERMINISTIC signer is a correctness *and* security
# problem (see THREAT_MODEL_AND_TRACEABILITY.md §7).
FALCON_DET1024_LIB=

# ── TestNet deployment (optional; deployment tooling only) ─────────────────────
# !!! THIS IS A PRIVATE KEY !!!
# An Algorand 25-word mnemonic controls its account outright. Anyone who reads it
# can spend from and act as that account.
#   - Use a dedicated, low-balance TESTNET account. Never a MainNet account.
#   - Never paste it into a terminal that logs, an issue, a PR, or a chat.
#   - In CI it is the `DEPLOYER_MNEMONIC` repository secret — do not put it in a file.
#   - If it is ever exposed, rotate the account immediately; assume funds are gone.
DEPLOYER_MNEMONIC=

# ── Test behaviour (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to make an unpopulated KAT fixture a FAILURE instead of a skip. CI sets
# this so a green run can never silently mean the byte-identity KAT was skipped.
TRELYAN_REQUIRE_KAT=
